#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172130 :knowledge-point/canonical-example {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186171710 :question/id #uuid "38dc8ce4-246d-54bd-a400-48c801d9387f" :question/math-academy-id "e-12344" :question/problem "$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_{D} \\boxed{ {\\phantom{A A A A A A A}}} \\: \\text{d}A\n$$\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z) = z-y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v) = \\big\\langle u^2, \\: -v, \\: v \\big\\rangle\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v) \\in D \\subseteq \\mathbb{R}^2,$ where $u \\geq 0.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\iint\\limits_S f(x,y,z) \\, \\textrm{d}S \n=\n\\iint\\limits_D f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) \\left\\|  \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\right\\|  \\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n\\| \\mathbf{r}'_u \\times \\mathbf{r}'_v \\| = 2\\sqrt{2}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z){:}$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(z-y)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=-v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =v-(-v) \\\\  & =2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}4\\sqrt{2}uv\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} :knowledge-point/id #uuid "e5256297-c928-54e3-bf4d-35f5734f5632" :knowledge-point/key-prerequisites [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048384 :topic/encompasses [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428363 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/multivariable-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1790->1112. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050101} :encompassing/weight 0.5} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186428364 :encompassing/rationale "Initial Codex estimate from captured target-band crossing frequency. Selected account multivariable: 1 rises / 2 eligible passed source activities = 0.500000; nearest selected fraction = 1/2. Crossing activity numbers [2]; waits [2]. Separate account estimates: multivariable=1/2 (1/2). Selection: most observations, then lower weight, then account name; no averaging. Single-activity estimates included. Intervening target updates: True. Crossing frequency is the chosen practical estimate of encompassing coverage; a multi-band rise counts once. This does not interpret color steps as physical repetition units. Method: encompassing-report.md. Evidence: reference/mathacademy/encompassing-analysis-2026-10-11/frequency-fractions/multivariable-frequency-estimates.json, pair 1790->315. All account evidence retained in the prepared import's selected-relationships.json." :encompassing/topic {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186048189} :encompassing/weight 0.5}] :topic/id #uuid "9ae6458d-ed13-5fa7