ef 17592186401200}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "25e44fde-444d-5880-ba2e-43dd4bc039db" :question/math-academy-id "q-160711" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xyz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}uv⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}v⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}1,\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & 0 & v \\\\ 0 & 1 & u\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & v \\\\ 1 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & v \\\\ 0 & u\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-v,\\hspace{0.222em}-u,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨-v,\\hspace{0.222em}-u,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-v)^{2}+(-u)^{2}+(1)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(xyz)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y=v\\,z=uv} \\\\  & =u\\cdot v\\cdot uv \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186172376 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0a6318e5-3878-5d26-b61b-739d349729a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} {:answer/id #uuid "2913e3a7-4834-5ae0-8725-8cf0ddd19bbe" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+uv+{u}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275848} {:answer/id #uuid "4635f4d0-2e93-54c6-a194-c7414540fea3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276098} {:answer/id #uuid "8e7629cd-993c-5b5b-a5b5-4827bb2f0380" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276769} {:answer/id #uuid "fa861672-33f6-547e-b490-0aa338df3abc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2(u+v)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277670}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0a6318e5-3878-5d26-b61b-739d349729a7" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275566} :answer-field/id #uuid "758915d5-fc00-56c4-ac7b-2a8b40d5ac5f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277935}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "a99cdea7-3ae5-5a3e-abca-eaac3de706cf" :question/math-academy-id "q-160712" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+y+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u-{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=2v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(x+y+z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=u-{v}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+(u-{v}^{2})+{v}^{2} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}2({u}^{2}+u)v\\sqrt{1+8{u}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278393 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "407b054a-ad2a-5003-b975-08ebe629a652" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({v}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276038} {:answer/id #uuid "4c0afc67-2eaf-50ff-a740-16da7f2c7971" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{3}+{v}^{3})\\sqrt{16{v}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276147} {:answer/id #uuid "533273b3-79e7-5ab4-8e9c-12dbf680ea3c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({v}^{2}+2u)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276214} {:answer/id #uuid "6262307b-481e-5435-ad06-56dd718d0e29" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u+v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276366} {:answer/id #uuid "ae06b05f-02ef-5a1f-88b5-160bedb18ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277041}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ae06b05f-02ef-5a1f-88b5-160bedb18ca3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277041} :answer-field/id #uuid "6e029e9e-eb95-5dc6-b173-809d27542530" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277920}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "0739fb8b-67dd-5c96-8b51-b9fe22150a63" :question/math-academy-id "q-161132" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xy+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}2v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(xy+z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z=2v} \\\\  & =u.{u}^{2}+2v \\\\  & ={u}^{3}+2v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}({u}^{3}+2v)\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}+4}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278394 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40de9f5d-9bb8-505f-856c-ce2c6913769b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276043} {:answer/id #uuid "9a30988f-5c27-5ce0-8684-641402fd6ea6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{4}{v}^{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276861} {:answer/id #uuid "c2412b0e-122f-55ad-9a36-81cdc271d082" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{2}{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277204} {:answer/id #uuid "d49654d0-756c-5b91-9e96-98d9917a2ace" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{3}{v}^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277349} {:answer/id #uuid "ea08dbc3-4809-5054-a017-c2a23b383426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277522}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ea08dbc3-4809-5054-a017-c2a23b383426" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8}\\,{u}^{5}{v}^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277522} :answer-field/id #uuid "e911c170-af03-582c-ad47-4ba84716458b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278135}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "3771f844-0efb-5152-bb73-0315652e05d3" :question/math-academy-id "q-161134" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{8}u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{y}^{2}{z}^{2})\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x={u}^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =({u}^{2}\\cdot {u}^{2})\\cdot {v}^{2}\\cdot {v}^{2}\\hspace{0.167em} \\\\  & ={u}^{4}{v}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}\\sqrt{8}\\hspace{0.167em}{u}^{5}{v}^{4}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278395 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "60908e82-b692-599f-82b9-892161866329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276341} {:answer/id #uuid "708462c8-f5ae-5b10-8bc2-cbaa9b1a5f89" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}-3(u-v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276492} {:answer/id #uuid "7755f123-28ec-560e-a4c0-0541364afe71" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276558} {:answer/id #uuid "7f3e8ea1-6b77-5aea-ae14-47ac28753c57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}-3({u}^{2}+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276632} {:answer/id #uuid "a35498bf-e5d4-5d74-b5ee-fd684180144f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276944}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "60908e82-b692-599f-82b9-892161866329" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276341} :answer-field/id #uuid "eebba4c6-890d-5236-a8b1-f85351eb3247" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278146}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "af99ff54-0eba-5a3e-990a-a1878cebaaed" :question/math-academy-id "q-161136" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-{x}^{2}+3yz$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}u+v,\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(-{x}^{2}+3yz)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y=u+v\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =-(u\\cdot u)+3\\cdot (u+v)\\cdot ({v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}(-{u}^{2}+3(u+v){v}^{2})\\sqrt{8{v}^{2}+1}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278462 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "02421d75-88be-52d7-b6a4-7091fc5bc066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u)\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275497} {:answer/id #uuid "37a3b016-ad87-55b8-92c0-56d4b344f479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv-u)\\sqrt{2u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275970} {:answer/id #uuid "4f430a34-697b-5af8-a53f-71af555ef03e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}v\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276184} {:answer/id #uuid "67494c52-64b3-56cb-b6c1-1db2880ed8b4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}{v}^{2}+2)\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276402} {:answer/id #uuid "f4d8f707-b205-57cd-849c-7a0bdc24dc3b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u{v}^{2}+u)\\sqrt{2u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277619}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "02421d75-88be-52d7-b6a4-7091fc5bc066" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u)\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275497} :answer-field/id #uuid "dc456dfe-3c1e-58f1-9083-307a9c6e88a7" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186278111}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d149ed70-6a6c-529d-a7c4-ab22e040de29" :question/math-academy-id "q-161285" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}{z}^{2}+y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨-u,\\hspace{0.222em}-u,\\hspace{0.222em}-v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ -1 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -1\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & -1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}{z}^{2}+y)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=-u\\,y=-u\\,z=-v} \\\\  & =(-u)^{2}\\cdot (-v)^{2}-u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}({u}^{2}{v}^{2}-u)\\sqrt{2}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278463 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0e8eb946-bade-52e7-a628-5f87cb28e35c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}+{v}^{2}+u)\\sqrt{8v}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275600} {:answer/id #uuid "12277fa3-1146-5aca-a0ac-a0f443b4ecd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}-2)\\sqrt{8}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275643} {:answer/id #uuid "905035c0-ecb9-5958-a0aa-abb13fc99ee9" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\sqrt{8}u" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276783} {:answer/id #uuid "aa693649-bf12-5748-af20-c60686051053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277010} {:answer/id #uuid "f72b9498-2b49-5473-af2a-31b5ee8fb2c3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}+2v+2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277637}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "aa693649-bf12-5748-af20-c60686051053" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277010} :answer-field/id #uuid "67ccc538-716e-5741-af32-020559500c0f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277908}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "d9e295ad-a9d0-5267-be9d-f4d887cdb7cb" :question/math-academy-id "q-161286" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-x-y-z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}-{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\hspace{0.222em}-2u,\\hspace{0.222em}1⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2}-{u}^{2}),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\hspace{0.222em}2v,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ 1 & -2u & 1 \\\\ 0 & 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}-2u & 1 \\\\ 2v & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}1 & -2u \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2u,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}2v⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨-2v,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}2v⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(-2v)^{2}+(0)^{2}+(2v)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{8}v.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(-x-y-z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=u\\,y={v}^{2}-{u}^{2}\\,z=u} \\\\  & =-u-({v}^{2}-{u}^{2})-u \\\\  & ={u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}({u}^{2}-{v}^{2}-2u)\\sqrt{8}v\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278464 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "6af8c537-e57b-5716-8d12-63fcd367dcd4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+uv)\\sqrt{2{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}-{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276437} {:answer/id #uuid "764eb8f7-0869-594c-952a-68e04921067e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(v-{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+2{v}^{4}+u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276545} {:answer/id #uuid "7b524c5d-049b-59c5-aed7-b77cbc36dee4" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{{v}^{2}-4{v}^{4}-{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276595} {:answer/id #uuid "dafd65c0-be97-5117-b59c-70e2892517b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277396} {:answer/id #uuid "fe7356ca-baea-56e4-9138-a82a9af96807" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+u{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}+{v}^{2}{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277711}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "dafd65c0-be97-5117-b59c-70e2892517b6" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277396} :answer-field/id #uuid "04191987-1090-56e3-a6b5-b166d86bb243" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277733}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "616b2956-33ca-5451-b2d1-058d45da4207" :question/math-academy-id "q-161290" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x-{y}^{2}z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨uv,\\hspace{0.222em}-u,\\hspace{0.222em}-{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(uv),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂u}(-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨v,\\hspace{0.222em}-1,\\hspace{0.222em}0⟩ \\\\ {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(uv),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-u),\\hspace{0.222em}\\frac{∂}{∂v}(-{v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}0,\\hspace{0.222em}-2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'} & =\\begin{vmatrix}\\mathbf{i} & \\mathbf{j} & \\mathbf{k} \\\\ v & -1 & 0 \\\\ u & 0 & -2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}-1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & -2v\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}-\\begin{vmatrix}v & 0 \\\\ u & -2v\\end{vmatrix},\\hspace{0.222em}\\begin{vmatrix}v & -1 \\\\ u & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2v,\\hspace{0.222em}2{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖ & =‖⟨2v,\\hspace{0.222em}2{v}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2v)^{2}+(2{v}^{2})^{2}+(u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $\\mathbf{r}(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v)) & =(x-{y}^{2}z)\\hspace{0.167em}{|}_{x=uv\\,y=-u\\,z=-{v}^{2}} \\\\  & =uv-(-u)^{2}\\cdot -{v}^{2} \\\\  & =uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\hspace{0.167em}\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(\\mathbf{r}(u,v))‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\hspace{0.167em}{\\color{blue}(uv+{u}^{2}{v}^{2})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+{u}^{2}}\\hspace{0.167em}}\\hspace{0.222em}\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414460 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "31c23b1e-7cd7-5e7a-8c99-254c33c9229b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414434} {:answer/id #uuid "b146a4db-c677-57ea-92f8-07f41239596d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414445} {:answer/id #uuid "b723dafe-f5a6-5a70-be14-953187b88dde" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414446} {:answer/id #uuid "c87217ff-e3d3-5223-ac71-463a0c197918" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{2}{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414448} {:answer/id #uuid "e4f2c71c-8604-5aa1-9ce7-1663a5f2e6db" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}+{v}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414453}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b146a4db-c677-57ea-92f8-07f41239596d" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "2\\sqrt{2}{u}^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414445} :answer-field/id #uuid "16fadbea-4516-5df4-9f64-8b7cc353d5a0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414455}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "26a444d6-a870-593f-bb03-1c02941c48b1" :question/math-academy-id "q-161124" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}u,\\hspace{0.222em}v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,1,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,0,\\,1⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 1 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}1 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨1,\\,-1,\\,0⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(1)^{2}+(-1)^{2}+(0)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+1+0} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =({x}^{2}+{y}^{2})\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u\\,z=v} \\\\  & ={u}^{2}+{u}^{2} \\\\  & =2{u}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,2\\sqrt{2}{u}^{2}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186414461 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0cd71aa2-2da0-53d3-a18e-57cc7dd66fe2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{u}^{2}(-{u}^{3}+{v}^{4})\\sqrt{4uv+u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414430} {:answer/id #uuid "6a78c70d-c252-5fa1-b3b9-b5253f7112ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{2}(-{u}^{3}-{v}^{4})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414437} {:answer/id #uuid "a93dd97e-74c6-56c8-a6b1-3cdadc7213e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{2}({u}^{4}-{v}^{3})\\sqrt{4{u}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414443} {:answer/id #uuid "cb42e303-0573-52db-81ce-d57e99e6f761" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "6{v}^{2}({u}^{2}+{v}^{4})\\sqrt{{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414449} {:answer/id #uuid "d505a7da-72d5-5c19-aa46-75ea67cf0bb1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "u(-{u}^{3}-{v}^{4})\\sqrt{4{v}^{3}+u}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414451}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6a78c70d-c252-5fa1-b3b9-b5253f7112ea" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3{u}^{2}(-{u}^{3}-{v}^{4})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414437} :answer-field/id #uuid "72a815fc-9d19-53b2-b0ae-b65abcc40317" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186414456}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "2c7beff7-ff72-566b-ae77-d272cca30605" :question/math-academy-id "q-161288" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=-x-{z}^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨{u}^{3},\\hspace{0.222em}v,\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}({u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨3{u}^{2},\\,0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}({u}^{3}),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}({v}^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,1,\\,2v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 3{u}^{2} & 0 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 2v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}0 & 0 \\\\ 1 & 2v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}3{u}^{2} & 0 \\\\ 0 & 1\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨0,\\,-6v{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨0,\\,-6v{u}^{2},\\,3{u}^{2}⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(0)^{2}+(-6v{u}^{2})^{2}+(3{u}^{2})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{36{v}^{2}{u}^{4}+9{u}^{4}} \\\\  & =3{u}^{2}\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(-x-{z}^{2})\\,{|}_{x={u}^{3}\\,y=v\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =-{u}^{3}-({v}^{2}\\cdot {v}^{2}) \\\\  & =-{u}^{3}-{v}^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,3{u}^{2}(-{u}^{3}-{v}^{4})\\sqrt{4{v}^{2}+1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186418479 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "059c12fe-eab5-50d3-812e-daede28e5fce" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-uv-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418466} {:answer/id #uuid "a69adeb6-2c36-5a75-b29d-f701876ba59a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}+v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418471} {:answer/id #uuid "cbbd9a36-5d62-5a45-a0b6-211a1e349cc3" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(u{v}^{2}-{v}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418473} {:answer/id #uuid "ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418474} {:answer/id #uuid "e264331f-dc93-54c6-bb93-c8cd29731c14" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418475}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ded9ba33-54e3-5794-92a9-b6db153210e8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(-u{v}^{2}-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418474} :answer-field/id #uuid "de80caed-f292-5fbc-ae6d-5bf6abf46eda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186418477}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e6c3f387-d028-56cc-8550-337dfde31023" :question/math-academy-id "q-161135" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=xz+y$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨u,\\hspace{0.222em}-v,\\hspace{0.222em}-{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(xz+y)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=-v\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =u\\cdot (-{v}^{2})+(-v) \\\\  & =-u{v}^{2}-v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(-u{v}^{2}-v)\\sqrt{1+4{v}^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186419401 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1796399c-8c6d-5f22-bede-36efd1a03f5a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "uv\\sqrt{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419395} {:answer/id #uuid "8e82d031-e34f-52ca-aadf-8e8d59c47bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419396} {:answer/id #uuid "bdf13d7f-d54d-59f5-9209-239de83443e0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(v+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{2}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419397} {:answer/id #uuid "bf1e4b2c-7a9b-5b87-a6e2-85dd90a414fd" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+{u}^{2})\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{2}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419398} {:answer/id #uuid "d04576fc-a1ab-5d09-bca6-54a80b70447c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "{v}^{2}\\sqrt{{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419399}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e82d031-e34f-52ca-aadf-8e8d59c47bb2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "(uv+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419396} :answer-field/id #uuid "39e51a49-d535-578a-8167-c77ca61f8305" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186419400}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "4970a05a-3173-5c58-8ea3-194b8fc59474" :question/math-academy-id "q-161133" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x+z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\n\\mathbf{r}(u,v)=⟨uv,\\hspace{0.222em}{u}^{2},\\hspace{0.222em}{v}^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{\\mathbb{R}}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression?\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{\\mathbf{r}}_{u}^{'}\\times {\\mathbf{r}}_{v}^{'}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x+z)\\,{|}_{x=uv\\,y={u}^{2}\\,z={v}^{2}} \\\\  & =uv+{v}^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,(uv+{v}^{2})\\sqrt{16{u}^{2}{v}^{2}+4{v}^{4}+4{u}^{4}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560308 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "81a4a4d4-c10a-55dc-b43b-8853d6f328f1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "128 u^{6} v^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560329} {:answer/id #uuid "8459c7ad-2f1c-54bb-b579-d98e4986a65b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{5} v^{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560330} {:answer/id #uuid "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{5} v^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560331} {:answer/id #uuid "99db7d55-0ba4-574a-abd0-fad22dde97d8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4 u^{4} v^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560332} {:answer/id #uuid "de54362b-6031-500a-b509-e99fd59af211" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{4} v^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560345}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "86ac4b28-467b-52f4-b7a3-2b20dd726a36" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "16 \\sqrt{2} u^{5} v^{4}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560331} :answer-field/id #uuid "24f470c7-3e68-5664-8116-49ea2082cafa" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560312}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "1d9ba2e0-102f-5ae7-abb7-4c8e12292bfc" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=x^{2} y^{2} z^{2}$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u^{2},\\,v,\\,v⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ Assume $u\\geq0.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=4 \\sqrt{2} u.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=4 \\sqrt{2} u.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(x^{2} y^{2} z^{2})\\,{|}_{x=2 u^{2}\\,y=v\\,z=v} \\\\  & =(2 u^{2}\\cdot 2 u^{2})\\cdot v^{2}\\cdot v^{2} \\\\  & =4 u^{4} v^{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,4 \\sqrt{2} u 4 u^{4} v^{4}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560315 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "030d3593-551c-5780-836c-e6aa7edd6559" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\left(8 v^{2} + 1\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560300} {:answer/id #uuid "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560307} {:answer/id #uuid "33bb8fed-592d-5e3a-8930-5d28957eefc1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1} \\left(- 4 u^{2} - v^{3} + v^{2} \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560317} {:answer/id #uuid "34bd55fd-9014-5837-a3ed-30210221cafa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1} \\left(- 4 u^{2} - 2 v^{3} + v^{2} \\left(u + v\\right)\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560318} {:answer/id #uuid "da65ba3f-7987-5418-bed4-7007a24d71df" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560342}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "1c567497-6459-5620-830a-356a99490e90" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560307} :answer-field/id #uuid "11fa6424-029e-5a79-821e-cb2a038e5fda" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560305}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2c8c277a-d40b-52fe-8295-ceb48a2d895c" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=- 4 x^{2} + y z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨u,\\,u + v,\\,v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$.\n\n*Hint: You can use the fact that $‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}.$*" :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nNotice that we are told that the norm of the fundamental vector product for our surface is\n\n$$\n‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖=\\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}.\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(- 4 x^{2} + y z)\\,{|}_{x=u\\,y=u + v\\,z=v^{2}} \\\\  & =-4\\cdot (u\\cdot u)+(u+v)\\cdot v^{2} \\\\  & =- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 4 u^{2} + 1 \\left(u + v\\right) v^{2}\\right) \\sqrt{8 v^{2} + 1}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560320 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "058e5939-7dca-5207-a9cf-7578532c3f28" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560302} {:answer/id #uuid "11a957d3-49ef-56db-ab0f-c02857167b9b" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560304} {:answer/id #uuid "1ef0898a-8678-542f-ad45-70587f8bbd8a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\left(52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}\\right)" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560309} {:answer/id #uuid "2b5c61b9-0f4d-5229-83c2-28dbe2298a06" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560314} {:answer/id #uuid "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560337}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "9f011f25-a217-5291-b94d-c478fcc9478a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560337} :answer-field/id #uuid "db2fc28a-c600-58d0-b8a2-e9ebeb14d152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560343}] :question/difficulty {:db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "3b4808cc-728c-55b7-90f8-734ae2943c4e" :question/problem "$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}\\boxed{}\\,\\text{d}A\n$$\n\nConsider the surface integral of the function \n$f(x,y,z)=3 x - y^{2} z$ \nover the parametric surface \n\n$$\nr(u,v)=⟨2 u v,\\,- 3 u,\\,2 u - 2 v^{2}⟩\n$$\n\nfor $(u,v)\\in D⊆{R}^{2}.$ What is the missing expression? Choose an integrand equal to the required expression as a function on $D$." :question/worked-solution "For a surface $S$ with parametrization $r(u,v)$ for $(u,v)\\in D,$ the surface integral of a scalar function $f$ over $S$ is given by\n\n$$\n{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWe first compute the tangent vectors to the grid curves:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂u},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂u}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂u}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 v,\\,-3,\\,2⟩ \\\\ {r}_{v}^{′} & =⟨\\frac{∂x}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂y}{∂v},\\,\\frac{∂z}{∂v}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u v),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(- 3 u),\\,\\frac{∂}{∂v}(2 u - 2 v^{2})⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2 u,\\,0,\\,- 4 v⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, the fundamental vector product is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′} & =\\begin{vmatrix}i & j & k \\\\ 2 v & -3 & 2 \\\\ 2 u & 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix} \\\\  & =⟨\\begin{vmatrix}-3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,-\\begin{vmatrix}2 v & 2 \\\\ 2 u & - 4 v\\end{vmatrix},\\,\\begin{vmatrix}2 v & -3 \\\\ 2 u & 0\\end{vmatrix}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nand \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖ & =‖⟨12 v,\\,4 u + 8 v^{2},\\,6 u⟩‖ \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(12 v)^{2}+(4 u + 8 v^{2})^{2}+(6 u)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNext, we substitute the coordinate expressions of $r(u,v)$ into $f(x,y,z):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(r(u,v)) & =(3 x - y^{2} z)\\,{|}_{x=2 u v\\,y=- 3 u\\,z=2 u - 2 v^{2}} \\\\  & =6 u v-1\\cdot (- 3 u)^{2}\\cdot (2 u - 2 v^{2}) \\\\  & =- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the surface integral can be written as \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{S}f(x,y,z)\\,\\text{d}S & ={∬}_{D}f(r(u,v))‖{r}_{u}^{′}\\times {r}_{v}^{′}‖\\text{d}A \\\\  & ={∬}_{D}\\,\\left(- 18 u^{3} + 18 u^{2} v^{2} + 6 u v\\right) \\sqrt{52 u^{2} + 64 u v^{2} + 64 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}\\,\\,\\text{d}A.\\end{aligned}\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186560324 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "03e2969c-7bc4-5828-b311-0b75c71bdde5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560301} {:answer/id #uuid "473df280-9c01-54be-9ab5-5f9b35d7d479" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\left(54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v\\right) \\sqrt{18 u^{2} + 24 u v^{2} + 16 v^{4} + 144 v^{2}}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186560322} {:answer/id #uuid "6f08a77f-a760-599a-8653-c3042e189d26" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "- 81 u^{3} + 54 u^{2} v^{2} + u v" :db/id 